# Path: the stages ahead, to the hardware's speed. Each stage names the evidence that closes it.

n: 7.2
name: stage-1-answers-and-encoding
kind: plan
is: The node encoding is fixed in writing (5.13) with 142 conformance vectors, 93 of them malformed, which the bootstrap's reader holds. Stage 1 closes when a second hand has written a reader from the page alone, in the grammar and kept as nodes (7.13), and the vectors hold in it. The whole encoding is written in form and holds the vectors, ids among them (5.14.51, 5.14.55), by the hand that wrote the page and the first reader. Who counts as a second hand is question 6.1.30.
status: inferred
from: 5.13 5.2.2 5.3.4 5.1.5 5.11.4 7.13 6.1.30 5.14.15 5.14.18 6.1.31
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.3
name: stage-2-floor
kind: plan
is: The C bootstrap under its budget: the framebuffer, store, canonical reader, walker, page birth and host table. It stands (5.14.10): the ground programs run, a frozen node thaws to the same id, a machine-code leaf runs both unsigned and under the hardened runtime, the build fails over its line count, and a second process records a live run and replays it. Symbol lookup and one raw call, which reach a framework as they reach the C library, are written (5.14.40), and the clock. It closes when a thread can be started.
status: inferred
from: 5.9.1 5.9.2 5.9.3 5.9.4 5.11.4 5.7.6
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.4
name: stage-3-home-lens
kind: plan
is: The home lens as rows written in the grammar, read forwards and printed backwards. Closes when the lens reads its own definition, prints it, and the reprint reads to the same nodes. A first lens, of words, leaves, names, five rows written in itself, signs between two and recipes that see the outer names, does that for itself (5.15.3 to 5.15.7). Every form is still in brackets, with no precedence and no pattern over text, so the surface of 5.3.5 is not built. Whether the stage is closed by this evidence is the guide's to say.
status: inferred
from: 5.3.2 5.3.5 5.3.3 5.15
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.5
name: stage-4-self-compile
kind: plan
is: The one-pass emitter written in the grammar compiles the compiler. Closes when the system regenerates its own seed byte for byte, cold and compiled runs print the same values over the whole core, and the walker is off the running path after the cold start. An emitter written in form stands (5.18): it compiles 207 of the repository's 377 definitions, 95 of its own 149 among them (5.18.10); no mark but a note and no recipe called as a value, so not yet the whole of itself.
status: inferred
from: 5.10.4 5.10.1 5.10.8 5.9.5 5.10.5 5.18
at: 2026-11-26

n: 7.6
name: stage-5-control-and-objects
kind: plan
is: Choice with commit, the trail, declared reversibility, the reference pair, composed parents and templates. Closes when the thesis example of a class with two parents runs as one composed shape with the view moving on a super-send, a failed option's effects are undone, and each of those tests has been turned red by a planted fault. Cells with a trail exist (5.14.34), and on them, in form, composed parents, the reference pair, send and super; an example of this repository's own meets those tests (5.16.2). Whether it stands for the thesis's is the guide's to say.
status: inferred
from: 5.4.6 5.4.7 5.4.8 5.4.9 5.5.1 5.5.2 5.5.5 5.11.1
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.7
name: stage-6-speed
kind: plan
is: The optimizing tier, then matrix instructions, then the GPU backend. Closes on measurements against optimized C for the same kernels on this machine, with lines of meaning and lines of speed reported apart.
status: inferred
from: 5.10.6 5.10.7 5.10.10
