n: 7.10
name: flows-first
kind: decision
is: The work follows end-to-end flows that really run, watched live through the framebuffer of 5.7.6. Ceremony around the work, the old body's doors, gates, receipts and bands, is left out.
status: given
see: 5.7.6
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.11
name: built-with-a-c-compiler-alone
kind: decision
is: This is a new repository and builds with a C compiler alone. The old body appears only as evidence that was read (hubs 2 and 3), never as a tool, a dependency or a step.
status: given
see: 5.9.1 2.1
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.12
name: each-stage-closes-on-a-watched-run
kind: plan
is: From stage 3 on, a stage closes on a real run of the thing it adds, recorded from a second process through the framebuffer and replayed, in addition to the evidence its own node names. 'make watch' is the first such run.
status: inferred
from: 7.10 5.7.6 5.11.3
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.13
name: guidance
kind: decision
is: Guidance we hold together, in short form. New code is written in form and kept as nodes; C is the bootstrap only, and no other language is written or stored. Every part can be replaced while the system runs, by a recipe, by machine code, by what comes next. The real work is preferred to a shortcut, and a running flow to a check. Guidance orients and is not enforced: what is aligned needs no permission, and what serves visibility, trust and sovereignty is done.
status: given
see: 7.10 7.11 8.14
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.24
name: code-that-holds
kind: decision
is: How code is written here so that it holds the first time. Facts are rows and choices are choices: a target, a template, a rule or a relation is a row, and where there is more than one way, ordered choice takes the first that holds. Records have named parts. A part that can fail or answer nothing is bound before it is used, since a list built with all keeps neither. A mistake of the code faults; a refusal fails and leaves a note. Jumps name labels, not offsets.
status: inferred
from: 7.13 7.22 5.19.22 5.19.26
see: 7.25
conf: mid
why: Three readers who ran the compiler graded it B- and found seven disagreements with frames. Each was a fact written twice, a part dropped without a word, or a jump counted by hand. Rewritten to these rules, the compiler agrees with frames over every case of 5.19.29.
flip: A standard held by reading alone drifts; read against it before a commit by someone who runs the code, it holds.
at: 2026-11-26

n: 7.25
name: a-new-path-comes-with-its-sweep
kind: decision
is: A new path comes with a ground program that runs it against its reference, the reference all the way down, over the boundaries of what it takes, and counts what it covered: how many cases, how many took the new path, how many it answered itself. The program is committed and runs in make check; a sweep run once in a session holds nothing.
status: inferred
from: 7.24 5.19.29 5.19.30
conf: mid
why: One ground program with two comparisons could not see the seven disagreements; the committed sweep of 5.19.29 saw them, and found two defects in the reference itself on its first run.
flip: A reference that shares the new path's defect agrees with it; a third reading would see it.
at: 2026-11-26

n: 7.26
name: checks-hold-meaning
kind: decision
is: make check runs every check and names the ones that failed together at the end. Each ground program runs in a process of its own and then all of them in one; shared memory is named for one run; a process that watches another waits until it stands. An expectation holds what a program means: its answer, that two ways agree, an invariant; never a size of code, a count of definitions, a label of coverage or a time.
status: inferred
from: 7.13 7.25 5.14.57
conf: mid
why: Of 46 commits that changed ground/expect.ck, 17 recorded again 43 values that moved with no change of meaning, sizes and counts; no standing line caught a defect later, while each of the six defects on record was found by a new comparison of two ways; one stored value held a defect in place until it was fixed.
flip: An expectation that holds only meaning can miss a fall in coverage; a count reported beside it, and read, keeps that in sight.
at: 2026-11-26

n: 7.21
name: every-part-swappable
kind: plan
is: The path to anything being exchanged while it runs. Done: one table says what runs for each operation, each recipe and the step (5.14.19, 5.14.24); an emitter in form compiles a recursion over numbers (5.18.1); the encoding and ice are programs (5.14.32); a watcher in form offers a hot recipe to the emitter (5.14.35); bindings from outside the run have their own scope, and a second process asks for one through the region (5.17.1, 5.17.2). Next: emitted code that keeps its values in the walker's frame, so it can stop at a node it does not know; then the continuation and undo.
status: inferred
from: 7.13 5.14.19 5.14.23 5.14.24 5.18.1 5.14.35 5.9.6
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.22
name: prelude-is-held-to-a-budget
kind: decision
is: Form written by position, with raw constants or as one long ladder is prelude. Prelude, like bootstrap code, stands only until it can be replaced, stays very limited and does not grow past the minimum. What is held: ground/reads-by-number.ck counts every read of a node's part by a bare number in the stored nodes, whatever names lie beside them, and make check fails when the count is over the budget in the Makefile, 475 on this day. The budget is lowered as code is rewritten and never raised.
status: given
see: 5.15.8 5.18.14 7.13
at: 2026-11-26

n: 7.23
name: the-engine-in-order
kind: plan
is: The order in which spec/nums.md is built, each step a real run. One: the catalogue as a node with its coordinates. Two: numbers with layouts, objects, frames, new, and the core recipes run as written: literals, locals, writes, math, compare, if, loops, return, call, member. Three: classes, parents, methods, interfaces; lists, dictionaries, strings. Four: templates. Five: exceptions, defer, and choice, fail and all with the trail. Six: lenses that write Go and BML. Seven: a lens that reads. Eight: code from rows. Nine: variation. Ten: package 0 retired.
status: inferred
from: 5.19 7.5 7.22
at: 2026-11-26
